                <pb facs="0584" n="519" sameAs="frus:frus1936v03/pg519"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">767.68119/901: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Yugoslavia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Wilson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Belgrade</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-04-29T17:00:00+01:00">April 29, 1936—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received April 29—2:20 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>16. Foreign Office yesterday handed note to Turkish Minister here stating that
                    although not a signatory to Straits Convention Yugoslav Government was prepared
                    to second Turkish demand for new agreement.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
